  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 731c81f8c77a80a40ba481bac402f8d9, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1dfcee1795c21fc40921050934eb1ed0, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: c2f3c3d2bb2b392459f79b1600b093a4, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 038d20084a8d0654b846630bcf1652d6, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 27dbe86a1eb4b48428228a20232c2f54, type: 2}
  statsTexts:
  - title: Stats
    entries:
    - heading: MIGHT
      body: 'Raw strength and toughness.


        Every point makes each hit land
        about 5% harder AND adds 16 hit points to the health bar.'
    - heading: EGO
      body: 'Stubborn pride and stage presence.


        Every point gives a 4%
        chance to shrug off most of the knockback in the middle of an attack. Proud
        fighters also lean toward picking up a shield.'
  - title: Stats
    entries:
    - heading: EDUCATION
      body: 'Book smarts and training.


        Every point adds about 5% more XP
        from a win and speeds up weapon training by roughly 6%. It does nothing in
        the swing itself; it pays off over a whole career.'
    - heading: INSIGHT
      body: 'Reading the fight.


        Every point sharpens crit chance (+0.5%)
        and crit damage (+1%), attack tempo (+2%), dodge (+2.5%) and shield-block
        (+3%) chances, and lets a fighter spot loose weapons from further away. Clever
        fighters like dual wielding.'
  - title: Weapon training
    entries:
    - heading: Every style
      body: You train a fighting style by landing hits and kills with it (duels train
        you faster). Every level of training adds +5% damage with that style. The
        top level is 10.
    - heading: One-handed
      body: Each level adds +1.5% chance to land a critical hit.
    - heading: Sword & shield
      body: Each level adds +2% chance to block with the shield.
  - title: Weapon training
    entries:
    - heading: Two-handed
      body: 'Each level adds +3% poise: a big weapon is harder to knock off balance.'
    - heading: Dual wield
      body: Each level adds +2% attack speed.
    - heading: Unarmed
      body: Each level adds +3% chance to dodge a blow.
  - title: Levels and fate
    entries:
    - heading: Level up
      body: Every level gives one free stat point. Spend it under Stats on the hub.
    - heading: Death
      body: In a deadly fight the loser dies, and is written into the Memento Mori.
        Duels never kill. The Rules of the Arena explain every kind of fight.
    - heading: Quality
      body: 'Pathetic, Normal, High quality or Elite: it is only a starting point.
        Quality does not decide a fighter''s fate.'
  - title: Luck
    entries:
    - heading: LUCK
      body: 'Some fighters are born lucky and some are not.


        Nobody knows
        exactly what luck does. The book will not say.'
  howToPlayTexts:
  - title: Rules of the Arena
    entries:
    - heading: The Arena
      body: The game is centered around Arena fighting. Pick your fighter, fight
        three battles, then choose between three different kinds of epic end-game
        fights.
    - heading: The Schedule
      body: Before every battle you choose one of three fights. Win to move on. A
        Duel counts too, win or lose.
    - heading: The Finale
      body: After three battles comes the Finale. Win it and you are crowned Champion,
        with a bonus stat point. Then a new schedule begins.
  - title: Duel
    entries:
    - heading: How it works
      body: One against one, and nobody dies. When a fighter has had enough, they
        kneel and the duel is over.
    - heading: Reward
      body: Half the XP of a normal win, and a little even if you lose. Weapon training
        grows faster in a duel.
    - heading: Good for
      body: Training, and a safe way forward. A finished duel counts as one of your
        three battles.
  - title: Death Match
    entries:
    - heading: How it works
      body: 'One against one, to the end. There is no yielding: the fight is over
        when someone falls.'
    - heading: Stakes
      body: The loser dies and is written into the Memento Mori. Your fighter is
        gone for good.
    - heading: Reward
      body: The full XP of a win, and the victory moves you closer to the Finale.
  - title: Group Fight
    entries:
    - heading: How it works
      body: You and a teammate against two opponents. The fight goes on if you fall,
        and ends when one whole team is down.
    - heading: If you fall
      body: 'If your team still wins, you live, but it counts as a loss: the schedule
        starts over and there is no XP. If your team falls too, you die.'
    - heading: Reward
      body: XP for every opponent beaten, a little less than in a one-on-one.
  - title: Boss Fight
    entries:
    - heading: Finale
      body: 'One of the three end-game fights. You face a Boss: one fighter of the
        best quality, tougher than you, and clever.'
    - heading: How it works
      body: One against one, to the death. A boss grows more furious as it is hurt,
        so do not get comfortable.
    - heading: Reward
      body: More XP than any single fight, and the crown of Champion. Lose, and you
        join the Memento Mori.
  - title: Group Death Match
    entries:
    - heading: Finale
      body: One of the three end-game fights. Your team of three stands against a
        team of three.
    - heading: How it works
      body: 'Same rules as a Group Fight: the battle goes on after you fall. But
        the stakes are higher, and it is the Finale.'
    - heading: Reward
      body: If your team wins, even if you fell, the Finale is won. If your team
        falls, so do you.
  - title: Last Hero Standing
    entries:
    - heading: Finale
      body: 'One of the three end-game fights. Five fighters, no teams: everybody
        fights everybody.'
    - heading: How it works
      body: Only one survives. Stay on your feet while the others wear each other
        down, and pick your moment.
    - heading: Reward
      body: The Champion's crown, and XP for every rival beaten. If you fall, the
        fight is lost.
  - title: Know Your Enemy
    entries:
    - heading: The brawlers
      body: Most foes just grab a weapon and rush you. They hit hard, but they are
        easy to read.
    - heading: The clever ones
      body: Better fighters circle, wait for you to slip, and strike back the moment
        you miss. Do not swing wildly.
    - heading: The bosses
      body: A boss fights like a clever one, and gets stronger as it loses health.
        It roars when it changes, and that is your moment.
  howToName: Arena Rules
  graveyardTitle: Memento Mori
